# Strahd on the road and at rest (docs/regions/strahd_presence.md; data/strahd/visits.json): the watcher on the
# ridge, the night visit at a Long Rest, and the test of strength on a night road. The test's fight is the visit's
# `then` (it starts when strahd_test is "fought"); he leaves it by the encounter's `withdraw`, then test_after plays.
# Voice: docs/voice/strahd.md. Courteous, patient, possessive; every kindness a threat, and every meeting leaves a mark.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The watcher (the first journey after the burial)

~ watcher
appear strahd
set strahd_watcher_seen
cutscene strahd_watcher
Narrator: The road bends under a bare ridge. Up on the skyline a rider sits a black horse, perfectly still, watching you go by.
if guest:ireena
Ireena [afraid]: Don't look at him. That's what he wants. Keep walking.
endif
interject class:ranger: High ground, downwind, in no hurry. Whoever taught him to hunt taught him well.
interject class:rogue: He isn't hiding. That's the part I don't like.
* Raise a hand to him. -> watcher_wave
* Stare back until he looks away. -> watcher_stare
* Keep walking. -> watcher_gone

~ watcher_wave
Narrator: After a moment the rider lifts a gloved hand in return. Then he closes it, one finger at a time, as if around something small.
approve wren_featherfoot +1: You waved at Strahd on the ridge
-> watcher_gone

~ watcher_stare
Narrator: He doesn't look away. In the end you do, to mind your footing, and when you look up again the ridge is bare.
approve thistle +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You stared Strahd down from the road
-> watcher_gone

~ watcher_gone
cutscene strahd_watcher_gone
Narrator: A ragged flock of bats lifts off the ridge and beats away south, toward the castle. Nobody is up there now.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The night visit (a Long Rest through the night)

~ night
appear strahd
cutscene strahd_camp
Narrator: You wake in the small hours and know at once you are not alone. Just past the last of the light, a tall man stands watching the others sleep.
if flag.strahd_met
Strahd: Do not get up. I only came to see how my guests are sleeping. Badly, I see. I have taken some trouble over that.
else
set strahd_met
Strahd: Do not get up. We have not been introduced. I am Strahd von Zarovich, and you are sleeping in my house. All of this is my house.
endif
if flag.strahd_letter_read
Strahd: You had my letter, I trust. You read it twice. You thought I would not know.
endif
if guest:ireena
Narrator: Ireena is sitting up, quite still, her eyes on him. Her hand is on her sword, and the hand isn't moving.
Strahd [smile]: Ireena. Such late hours. Shall I wait while you decide whether to scream?
Ireena [angry]: I've decided. Get away from us.
endif
-> night_kneel

# He calls one sleeping companion to him (never the one on watch: leader:), lets them go, and asks them nothing. Their
# camp talk the next time the party rests: narrative/camp/<them>.dialogue, `knelt`.
~ night_kneel
if name:liriel_dawnsong and not leader:name:liriel_dawnsong
set strahd_knelt = "liriel_dawnsong"
Strahd: Liriel. Wake up, priestess. Come here and kneel. You know how; you do it every morning.
Narrator: Liriel opens her eyes. She gets up out of her blankets and crosses the camp to him barefoot over the cold ground, and her face is calm and quite empty, the way it is at prayer.
elif name:godrick_pendlebrook and not leader:name:godrick_pendlebrook
set strahd_knelt = "godrick_pendlebrook"
Strahd: Godrick. Up, squire. Your lord is calling you.
Narrator: Godrick gets up at once, the way he would for Sir Pellam, and walks to him across the camp with his sword left lying in the grass. His eyes are open. Nobody is behind them.
elif name:thistle and not leader:name:thistle
set strahd_knelt = "thistle"
Strahd: Thistle. Here, girl. Heel.
Narrator: Thistle comes up out of sleep on all fours and goes to him low and quick, the way a dog goes to its master. Her eyes are open and empty.
elif name:wren_featherfoot and not leader:name:wren_featherfoot
set strahd_knelt = "wren_featherfoot"
Strahd: Wren. Little monk. Your master is not here to tell you no. Come.
Narrator: Wren rolls out of his blanket and walks to him, perfectly balanced, perfectly silent, his face as blank as a fresh page.
elif name:kip_smudgewick and not leader:name:kip_smudgewick
set strahd_knelt = "kip_smudgewick"
Strahd: Kip. Merchant. Come here. I want to inspect the goods.
Narrator: Kip gets up and walks to him with his straw hat in his hands, the way he'd go to a customer, smiling a little. The smile is the worst part. It isn't his.
elif name:ratatoille and not leader:name:ratatoille
set strahd_knelt = "ratatoille"
Strahd: Ratatoille. Come here, little cook. I am told you wish to be taken seriously.
Narrator: Ratatoille sits up, folds his blanket into a neat square, and walks to him across the camp with his face as smooth and empty as a clean plate.
elif name:tamsin_tealeaf and not leader:name:tamsin_tealeaf
set strahd_knelt = "tamsin_tealeaf"
Strahd: Tamsin. Bring me what you stole, little thief.
Narrator: Tamsin gets up with the silver locket already open in his hand. He walks to Strahd and holds it up on his flat palm, the way you'd offer a horse a sugar lump, and his eyes are empty.
elif name:ilse_varga and not leader:name:ilse_varga
set strahd_knelt = "ilse_varga"
Strahd: Sergeant Varga. Fall in. Your company did, at the end.
Narrator: Ilse is on her feet before she is awake. She marches to him in step, halts, and goes down on one knee as stiffly as a soldier at a graveside.
elif name:hedda_ironvow and not leader:name:hedda_ironvow
set strahd_knelt = "hedda_ironvow"
Strahd: Hedda. Healer. Come here, and bring your hands.
Narrator: Hedda gets up, mail and all, and walks to him with her hands held out in front of her, open and empty, like her eyes.
elif name:silvain_aster and not leader:name:silvain_aster
set strahd_knelt = "silvain_aster"
Strahd: Silvain. Scholar. Come here. You may take notes, if you like.
Narrator: Silvain rises and walks to him with the slow, careful steps of someone carrying a full cup, and their face is as empty as a page nobody has written on.
else
set strahd_knelt = "someone"
Strahd: You. The one asleep nearest the fire. Come here.
Narrator: One of the sleepers rises and walks to him across the camp with open, empty eyes.
endif
Narrator: At his feet they kneel, and tilt their head to one side to bare their throat to him, as patient as a horse waiting for the bridle.
Strahd: There. That is how little it takes. I wanted you to see it, before you decide to fight me.
Narrator: He lays two fingers on the pulse in their neck, the way a buyer feels a horse's leg, and takes his hand away. They wake on their knees on the cold ground with a hand at their throat, and scramble back to the fire.
-> night_menu

~ night_menu
* Wake the others. -> night_wake
* What do you want? -> night_want
* [if guest:ireena] Get up and stand between him and Ireena. -> night_shield
* [Insight DC 16] Watch for what he isn't saying. -> night_read | night_read_failed
* [Cleric] Hold up your holy symbol. -> night_ward
* [Paladin] Hold up your holy symbol. -> night_ward
* Attack him. -> night_attack

~ night_want
Strahd: Tonight? To learn you. Which of you sleeps lightly. Which sleeps with a hand on a knife. Which one the others would die for. I will need to know that, later.
-> night_menu

~ night_read
set strahd_seen_trapped
Narrator: You catch it as he glances past you at the mountains: the look of a man at a window that will not open. Then it's gone.
Strahd: You stare, guest. Is something the matter with my face?
-> night_menu

~ night_read_failed
Narrator: His face gives you nothing at all. It is a very good face for that. He looks back as if you were the one being read.
-> night_menu

~ night_wake
set strahd_night_visit = "woke"
Narrator: You shout. The others come up out of sleep with weapons in their hands, and there is nobody there. The fire has burned down to blue.
approve kip_smudgewick +1: You woke the camp when Strahd came
-> END

~ night_shield
set strahd_night_visit = "shield"
Strahd [smile]: Gallant. Do you know how many gallant men have stood exactly there? I stopped counting them. I did not stop killing them.
Narrator: He bows to Ireena, not to you, and the dark he stood in is only dark.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +3 thistle +1: You got up and stood between Strahd and Ireena
-> END

~ night_ward
set strahd_night_visit = "warded"
Narrator: The symbol catches the last of the firelight. He doesn't flinch. He looks at it the way one looks at a candle in a neighbour's window.
Strahd: Keep it lit. It is the only light for a mile, and every hungry thing in my woods can see it. Good night.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You held up your holy symbol to Strahd in the dark
-> END

~ night_attack
set strahd_night_visit = "attacked"
Narrator: Your blade goes through him like a hand through fog, and the fog is cold enough to ache.
Strahd: In a man's own house. I will remember that. Sleep, if you can. I will be watching to see which of you does.
approve thistle +1 kip_smudgewick -1: You swung at Strahd by the campfire
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The test of strength (a night road, level 7+)

~ test
appear strahd
cutscene wolves_part
Narrator: Eyes in the dark ahead, a dozen pairs, low to the ground. The wolves part, and a man in black walks out between them as if through a garden.
Strahd: Good evening. I hear you are becoming formidable. I like to see such things for myself. Indulge me.
if guest:ireena
Strahd: Ireena, stand aside, please. This is between your friends and me.
Ireena [angry]: Then you'll have to go through me as well.
endif
if flag.strahd_road_encounter == "violent"
Strahd [smile]: You drew on me once, on this very road. I said not here. I have changed my mind.
endif
* Draw steel. -> test_fight
* [Persuasion DC 18] Tell him a brawl on a muddy road is beneath a lord. -> test_talked | test_talk_failed

~ test_fight
set strahd_test = "fought"
Strahd [smile]: Splendid. Do not die too quickly. I should have to find new guests, and the valley is so short of them.
approve thistle +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You drew steel when Strahd tested you on the road
-> END

~ test_talk_failed
set strahd_test = "fought"
Strahd [smile]: Beneath me? Everything here is beneath me. That is the point of a castle. Begin.
-> END

~ test_talked
set strahd_test = "talked"
Strahd: Beneath me. Yes. You are learning how I think, and that is the first step to being mine. Another night, then, with better light.
Narrator: He whistles once, as a man calls a dog, and the wolves go back into the trees with him.
approve wren_featherfoot +1 liriel_dawnsong +1 ratatoille +1: You talked Strahd out of a brawl in the mud
-> END

~ test_after
set strahd_withdrew
Narrator: Fog rolls across the road, and he is inside it, and then there is only fog. His voice comes from everywhere at once.
Strahd: Better than I hoped. Not yet what you will need. Do keep practising.
if guest:ireena
Ireena [angry]: Coward!
Strahd: Patient, my dear. There is a difference. You will learn it.
endif
-> END
